      "context": "chapel_front_wall_cladding",
      "verificationLevel": "partial",
      "prompt": "The front wall of a small chapel is a rectangle $12$ m wide and $4$ m tall, topped by an isosceles triangular gable on the same base. Each sloping edge of the gable is $10$ m long. A round window of radius $1$ m is cut into the wall. Using $\\pi = 3.14$, how many square meters of cladding cover the wall? Give the answer in square meters, rounded to two decimal places.",
