      "prompt": "A cylindrical rooftop rainwater cistern holds $452.16$ m$^3$ and is $9$ m tall. Only its curved side will be painted. One can of paint covers $15$ m$^2$, and only whole cans are sold. Using $\\pi = 3.14$, how many cans must be bought?",
